cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this bench in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Retrieval Abstention Bench"
abstract: >-
  A benchmark for a retrieval or memory layer that must decide whether to answer
  or to decline. Questions are frozen with a sha256 manifest and threshold rules
  recorded before any result; unanswerable questions are constructed by swapping
  an entity anchor under a distance rule rather than written by hand; and a leak
  check reports how much of each question is still verbatim source text. No LLM
  is involved anywhere in the harness.
